Initial recreation of b200-workspace-sync as a repository-wide two-way-safe
session reported 60 conflicts. After excluding build, gate, cache, and bytecode
artifacts, the remaining costmodel differences were the M3 files changed after
the prior session lost connectivity. Direct diffs of runner.py, copy.py,
copy.cu, and store.py confirmed that beta held the earlier interrupted-session
versions, including the obsolete TMA label and cooperative-copy II kernel.

The prior beta costmodel and M3 documents were backed up before replacement:

  /tmp/tilefoundry-costmodel-pre-m3-sync-20260811T094806Z.tar.gz
  cf4b2cf9ddbd7dae61bca69b5be242e257ad023886f4f4ee52ba198e2299cf02

The active session was then recreated as a scoped one-way replica:

  alpha: /Users/mi/Desktop/b200_workspace/TileFoundry/costmodel
  beta:  node14:~/workspace/TileFoundry/costmodel

Generated build, gate, cache, egg-info, __pycache__, and *.pyc paths are
